<title>SWITZERLAND: TABLE-Swiss ABB H1 profit falls.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Swiss ABB H1 profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>BADEN, Switzerland 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30:</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net profit	     112		 vs 139</p>
<p> Income before taxes	  140		 vs 176</p>
<p>Operating earnings after</p>
<p> depreciation		   132		 vs 171</p>
<p> Revenue			  2,380	     vs 2,594</p>
<p> Orders received		3,057	     vs 2,266</p>
<p> Orders-in-hand		 5,655	     vs 5,159</p>
<p> Capital expenditure	  66		  vs 69</p>
<p> Number of employees	  11,004	    vs 10,786</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is ABB Switzerland, a unit of Zurich-based electrical engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
